//@version=6
indicator("UDB-ORB TSLA v3.9.1 - A1/B1/C1/C2/D1 Profiles", shorttitle="UDB-ORB v3.9.1", overlay=true, max_labels_count=500)

// v3.9.1 2026-07-28 — DOCUMENTATION ONLY (no logic, no input, no alert, no plot change). Records a
//   concept tested and REJECTED 2026-07-28, so it is not re-proposed from the chart:
//   IMMEDIATE REVERSAL ON THE BE-STOP BAR — flip at the same 5m close the BE stop fills at,
//   instead of waiting for a close back through the raw opposite OR boundary (the current rule).
//   Asked from a live chart where the flip would have worked; built as the Python enhancement
//   reversal_capture.immediate_on_be_stop (default OFF) and swept on ALL FIVE profiles.
//   It roughly DOUBLES the reversal count (198 -> 374 over 5yr) while total reversal P&L FALLS
//   (+145.6 -> +79.8/unit) — the ~176 extra flips are collectively net-negative. The best variant
//   beat baseline on 2024-2026 WINDOW TOTALS in every profile (A1 +17.6, B1 +17.6, C1 +5.7,
//   C2 +28.0, D1 +23.4) — but per YEAR it loses 2022, 2023 AND 2024 in every profile:
//     delta/unit vs base, sum of A1+B1+C1+C2+D1:
//     2022 -78.8 | 2023 -151.7 | 2024 -56.0 | 2025 +109.5 | 2026YTD +38.9   (2022-23 = true OOS)
//   The whole "edge" is 2025. Trailing 2 months negative in all five (A1/B1/D1 -2.8, C1 -3.5,
//   C2 -0.2); D1's 5yr maxDD degrades -56.1 -> -66.6. Same 2025-only regime signature that killed
//   the midline-trigger reversal (v-note below / config.yaml). Profile choice cannot rescue it:
//   all five share ONE entry engine and differ only in the runner exit, so the flip lands on the
//   identical set of BE-stop bars (hence near-identical deltas on A1/B1/D1).
//   DO NOT RE-ADD. The OR-break wait is a FILTER, not latency — crossing the whole range is what
//   distinguishes a genuine failed breakout from chop INSIDE the range, and the reversal's own
//   stop is only meaningful once price has crossed it. (Structural note: a BE-stop fill often
//   lands inside/below the OR, which would put the normal reversal stop on the WRONG side of
//   entry and let the risk-parity cap inflate size absurdly.)
//   Reproduce: python scripts/immediate_reversal_test.py --profiles all --years [--windows|--detail]
//   Full analysis: docs/BE_STOP_ANALYSIS.md §31.
// v3.9 2026-07-26 — ENTRY CUTOFF ADOPTED (default ON, 12:00): loss-anatomy on 5 years of trades
//   showed post-noon entries are a net-NEGATIVE cohort (the 12:00-13:00 lunch hour is the toxic
//   pocket; losing stops die in ~30min while winners run for hours). No NEW entries — primary or
//   reversal — after 12:00; open positions still manage to their normal exits. Verified on
//   A1/B1/C1/D1 incl 2022-23 OOS: WR up in every tested year-cell, net +3-4% (B1 5yr +463.4 vs
//   +450.7/unit), worst day never worse (2025's improves −10.9 vs −12.0). Python twin:
//   enhancements.time_window {start 09:35, end 12:00} enabled in the A1/B1/C1/D1 + default yamls.
//   Knob re-sweep same day: stop cap $5, BE trigger 0.55, BE trail $0.25 all confirmed optimal
//   (BE 0.85 buys ~+4pt WR but costs $65/3yr and deeper tails — not taken).
// v3.8 2026-07-25 — version bump in lockstep with the STRATEGY's "Option quantity mode" input
//   (options webhook can omit quantity so TradersPost's dollar-based position sizing decides the
//   contract count — the +49-63% fixed-$ sizing finding). THIS INDICATOR NEEDED NO CHANGE (its
//   alerts are plain text, no webhook JSON). Bumped only so chart + alerts show matching names.
// v3.7 2026-07-24 — CONFIGURABLE SHARE QUANTITY (user request, mirrors the Option-contracts input):
//   new "Share quantity (shares per 1.0 unit)" input (default 25 = the old hardcoded scale).
//   INDICATOR: entry / reversal / partial alerts now state the exact share count to place
//   (reversal = risk-parity scaled, partial = partialPct of the position); summary table adds a
//   "Net @ N sh" dollar row. STRATEGY: the old "Shares per 'unit'" input is RENAMED "Share quantity"
//   — order qty and webhook JSON quantity = Units Per Trade x this (reversal: risk-parity x this).
//   Keep the indicator and strategy inputs EQUAL. No trade-logic change anywhere.
// v3.6 2026-07-23 — D1 EXIT MODE OPTION (user request, like the C2 formula input): new "D1 Exit
//   mode" input — "Partial TP + ATR Trail" (default, the original D1) vs "FULL EXIT AT ATR TRAIL":
//   nothing is taken at the adaptive TP (its touch only ARMS the trail), 100% exits on the TRADE
//   TASTIC flip — one alert / one order, so it also suits platforms that cannot split exits.
//   Tested (per unit, fixed trail, close-stop) full-trail vs partial: 2024 +39.7 vs +38.4 |
//   2025 +85.2 vs +72.2 | 2026YTD +179.0 vs +162.3 -> full-trail wins ALL THREE (3yr +304 vs +273;
//   B1 ref +268) at a slightly deeper 2025 worst day (-13.6 vs -12.0) and ~1pt lower WR.
//   Python twin: tsla_config_D1.yaml with partial_qty_pct: 0.0.
// v3.5 2026-07-23 — C2 TAKE-PROFIT FORMULA CHANGED (user request): C2's target is now the OPEN
//   BAR's High - Low (= OR width, no floor/scale) instead of the fixed $2. Per unit, close-stop,
//   OR-width vs fixed-$2: 2022 +29.7 vs +42.9 | 2023 +82.3 vs +88.8 | 2024 +36.6 vs -23.1 |
//   2025 +38.3 vs -0.3 | 2026YTD +111.7 vs +49.0  => 5yr +298.6 vs +157.3 (~2x), POSITIVE EVERY
//   YEAR (the fixed $2 was net-NEGATIVE 2024 and flat 2025 under the close stop). WR drops
//   (46-50% vs 50-63%): fewer tiny banked wins, bigger targets on wide-OR days. TP floors $1/$2
//   tested: no effect. The old behavior stays selectable: "C2 Take-Profit formula" = Fixed $.
// v3.4 2026-07-23 — D1 SHORT-SIDE FIX (user-caught same day on the live chart): the original
//   TRADE TASTIC script has ONE line — a SHORT must exit on the red->green flip of the SAME
//   HHV(high - mult*ATR) line, not on an invented mirrored LLV(low + mult*ATR) line. On 2026-07-23's
//   short the true flip was 10:35 (close 324.30 > TS 319.48); the mirror exited 11:55. Fixed in this
//   indicator, the v3.4 STRATEGY, and the Python engine (all now single-line, longs unchanged).
//   CORRECTED numbers, per unit, D1 vs B1: 2024 +38.4 vs +20.2 | 2025 +72.2 vs +102.8 |
//   2026YTD +153.9 vs +138.0 -> 3yr ~tie (+264 vs +261). D1 wins 2024+2026, loses 2025;
//   still experimental / NOT adopted — VWAP (B1/C1) stays the traded runner exit.
// v3.3 2026-07-23 — NEW PROFILE D1 (experimental, for side-by-side comparison — NOT adopted):
//   D1 = Adaptive TP + 25% partial + "TRADE TASTIC" ATR TRAIL runner (B1's engine, the
//   runner exits on the TRADE TASTIC color flip instead of the VWAP cross). Python twin:
//   config/tsla_config_D1.yaml (enhancement atr_trail_exit). (v3.3's short side + numbers were
//   the buggy mirror — superseded by the v3.4 fix above.)

// v3.2 2026-07-23 — version bump in lockstep with the STRATEGY's partial-as-order option (Shares mode:
// the 25% partial can fire as an opposite-side order JSON — long -> action=Sell qty N, short -> Buy — for
// execution platforms whose action=exit ALWAYS flattens the whole position and ignores quantity; the
// platform must NET, not reverse). THIS INDICATOR NEEDED NO LOGIC CHANGE: its alerts are plain text.
// PARTIAL VALUE (tested 2026-07-23, per unit): forced one-time exit AT the TP costs most of the edge
// (B1 2025 +38.9 vs +102.8 w/ partial; C1 2025 +9.0 vs +77.4) — the money is the 75% runner, not the WR.
// Partial % = 0 (nothing off, 100% rides the runner) beat the 25% partial in 2025 AND 2026 on all profiles
// (A1 2026 +188.4 vs +167.8) at ~2-4pt lower WR; ~equal 2024 A1/C1, worse B1 2024 (+14.5 vs +20.2). It is
// the best SINGLE-EXIT fallback when a partial order can't work; 25% partial stays the adopted default.

// v3.1 2026-07-21 — version bump in lockstep with the STRATEGY's Options-alert fix (the strategy's
// Options-mode 25% partial sent alert_message=na -> TV emitted the literal "{{strategy.order.alert_message}}"
// placeholder). THIS INDICATOR NEEDED NO LOGIC CHANGE: its alerts are plain-text alert()/alertcondition()
// messages (no webhook placeholder). Bumped only so chart + alerts show matching v3.1 names.

// STATUS 2026-07-19 (validation update) — CORRECTED 2026-07-24: the rival "3-bot" concept (15m-OR long
// ATM ±50% + 30-min time stop, from the SPX system) originally showed +$45,916 @1ct on TSLA — that was
// ENTIRELY the bar-START pricing lookahead. Barclose-corrected on the same OPRA quotes: TSLA 3-bot is
// NEGATIVE (BOT1 -$2,295 @1ct 2022-26, WR 44%; spread bots all negative too) — UDB stays the TSLA
// system, now unambiguously. Credit spreads DON'T work on TSLA (thin credits, $2.50 strikes, weekly
// expiry) — don't sell them here. (The old day-of-week claims here predate the barclose correction —
// see the corrected UDB options stats in docs/TRADERSPOST_OPTIONS.md before using them.)
// The SPX system lives in SEPARATE files: SPX_ORB_3BOT_v1(.pine/_strategy.pine).
// STATUS 2026-07-13: ONE indicator, FOUR selectable profiles (fires ALERTS; identical logic to the v3
// STRATEGY). TSLA 5-minute, RTH, OR start 09:30 (selectable). Fires ALERTS + a PER-UNIT summary table;
// the STRATEGY carries the sizing ($10,000 account / 25 shares default). Same entry engine, ADOPTED
// close-triggered stops (exitOnClose ON), vol/OR gates, risk-parity reversal for all. Differ ONLY in exit:
//   A1 = Adaptive TP + 25% partial + PEAK-TRAIL runner   (Max Stop $5)
//   B1 = Adaptive TP + 25% partial + VWAP-CROSS runner   (Max Stop $5)
//   C1 = ATR-target (0.25x14d ATR) + 25% partial + VWAP  (Max Stop $6)   <- best PF
//   C2 = OR-WIDTH target (open bar H-L), FULL exit (no partial/runner) (Max Stop $5)  [was fixed $2 pre-v3.5]
//  ADOPTED RESULTS (close-triggered stop = exitOnClose ON; net per 1 UNIT; x25 = strategy on $10k, x100 = @100sh):
//  FULL 2022-2026 -> A1 +432.7/u (+108% on $10k), B1 +450.3/u (+113%), C1 +414.8/u (+104%), C2 +175.3/u (+44%).
//  PF: A1 1.22 / B1 1.23 / C1 1.22 / C2 1.12.   MaxDD on $10k: A1 -16% / B1 -19% / C1 -19% / C2 -17%.
//  USER TRADES B1 (max net) + C1 (best PF/DD balance). CLOSE-triggered stop = +42-46% net vs the old wick
//  stop, DD -40%, and 2024 FLIPS to a profit (OOS-confirmed on 2022-23). Set exitOnClose OFF for the old wick.
//  5m OR is CONFIRMED optimal (15m OR tested 2026-07-16 = worse in every profile/period: enters after the thrust).
//  OPTIONS (TradersPost 0DTE) live in the v3 STRATEGY, not here (this indicator has no orders/positions):
//    set Order asset=Options there. Works on ALL profiles (the 25% partial's webhook is auto-suppressed so
//    1 contract rides to the runner exit); default 2 contracts. Real 0DTE backtest @1ct, barclose
//    fills, 2025-01..2026-07-17 (UPDATED 2026-07-25 — now includes D1 and the OR-width C2):
//    A1 +$12,895 / D1 +$11,284 / B1 +$11,241 / C1 +$10,059 / C2 +$4,246. 2026 YTD ranking:
//    A1 +$8,971 > D1 +$7,499 > B1 +$5,840 > C1 +$4,628 > C2 +$2,417 — matches the shares ranking.
//    NOTE: the v3.5 OR-width TP flipped C2's options POSITIVE (old fixed-$2 C2 was -$967, "dead").
//    A1/D1 lead on options; size to these numbers (~$16-56/trade avg depending on profile/year).
//    Expiry (strategy input): 0DTE vs WEEKLY tested — WEEKLY (nearest Friday) ~3-5% MORE net (less theta on 2-3h
//    holds), +22% premium. NOTE: TSLA lists only ~Mon/Wed/Fri expiries (no dailies, unlike SPX) — use the strategy's
//    'Friday (weekly)' expiration choice (dynamic days-to-Friday); a fixed +2/+3 days rolls into next week from Wed on.
//    This indicator's alerts stay human-readable text + per-profile alertcondition()s (no webhook JSON).
//=============================================================================================

// ==================== PROFILE ====================
profile = input.string("C1 · ATR 0.25 + 25% Partial + VWAP", "Profile",
     options=["A1 · Adaptive + Peak-Trail", "B1 · Adaptive + VWAP", "C1 · ATR 0.25 + 25% Partial + VWAP", "C2 · OR-Width Full-Exit", "D1 · Adaptive + ATR-Trail (exp)"], group="Profile")
c2TPFormula = input.string("OR width (open bar High-Low)", "C2 Take-Profit formula", options=["OR width (open bar High-Low)", "Fixed $"], group="Profile", tooltip="ADOPTED v3.5 (default): C2's target = the OPEN BAR's High - Low (= OR width, no floor). vs the old fixed $2 (per unit, close-stop): 2024 +36.6 vs -23.1, 2025 +38.3 vs -0.3, 2026YTD +111.7 vs +49.0; 2022/23 slightly behind; 5yr ~2x and positive every year. 'Fixed $' = the pre-v3.5 C2 (uses the Fixed TP $ input).")
d1ExitMode = input.string("Full exit at ATR Trail", "D1 Exit mode", options=["Full exit at ATR Trail", "Partial TP + ATR Trail"], group="Profile", tooltip="D1 only. 'Full exit at ATR Trail' (DEFAULT since 2026-07-23; the Python forward test tracks it) = NOTHING is taken at the TP — its touch only ARMS the trail; 100% exits on the flip (one alert, one order; suits platforms that cannot split exits). 'Partial TP + ATR Trail' = the original D1: 25% off at the adaptive TP, 75% rides the flip. v3.6 test (per unit, fixed trail): full-trail beats the partial in all of 2024/25/26 (+39.7/+85.2/+179.0 vs +38.4/+72.2/+162.3) at a slightly deeper 2025 worst day (-13.6 vs -12.0).")
isA1 = str.startswith(profile, "A1")
isB1 = str.startswith(profile, "B1")
isC1 = str.startswith(profile, "C1")
isC2 = str.startswith(profile, "C2")
isD1 = str.startswith(profile, "D1")
tpModeSel  = isC2 ? (str.startswith(c2TPFormula, "Fixed") ? "Fixed" : "ORw") : isC1 ? "ATR" : "Adaptive"
d1FullTrail = isD1 and str.startswith(d1ExitMode, "Full")   // D1 full-trail: TP touch only arms; 100% exits on the flip
usePartial = not isC2
runnerVWAP = isB1 or isC1              // D1 = ATR chandelier trail runner (neither VWAP nor peak-trail)

// ==================== INPUTS ====================
grpS = "Session"
eodHour = input.int(15, "EOD Exit Hour", minval=0, maxval=23, group=grpS)
eodMin  = input.int(50, "EOD Exit Minute", minval=0, maxval=59, group=grpS)
orStart = input.string("09:30", "Opening Range start bar", options=["09:30", "09:45"], group=grpS)
entryCutOn = input.bool(true, "Entry cutoff — no NEW entries after the time below", group=grpS, tooltip="ADOPTED 2026-07-26 (default ON, 12:00): entries after noon were a net-NEGATIVE cohort in 5 years of trade data — the damage concentrates in the 12:00-13:00 lunch hour. Blocking NEW entries (primary AND reversal; open positions still manage to their normal exits) after 12:00: WR up in all 7 tested year-cells on B1/D1 (+A1/C1 confirmed), net +3-4% (B1 5yr +463 vs +451/unit), worst day never worse, 2025's improves. OFF = trade all day (pre-cutoff behavior).")
entryCutH  = input.int(12, "Entry Cutoff Hour", minval=9, maxval=15, group=grpS)
entryCutM  = input.int(0,  "Entry Cutoff Minute", minval=0, maxval=59, group=grpS)

grpR = "Risk / Regime Gates"
maxORWidth  = input.float(8.0,  "Max OR Width ($) — skip wider days", step=0.5, group=grpR)
volLookback = input.int(20,     "Volatility Lookback (days)", minval=2, group=grpR)
maxRvolPct  = input.float(4.92, "Max Prior Realised Daily Vol (%)", step=0.01, group=grpR)

grpE = "Entry"
bufferPctOR = input.float(10.0, "Breakout Buffer (% of OR width)", step=0.5, group=grpE)
tradeQty    = input.float(1.0,  "Units Per Trade", minval=0.01, group=grpE)
shareQty    = input.int(25,     "Share quantity (shares per 1.0 unit)", minval=1, group=grpE, tooltip="v3.7: your FIXED share size, configured here like the strategy's Option-contracts input. Primary trade = Units Per Trade x this (default 1.0 x 25 = 25 sh); the risk-parity reversal scales off it. Entry/reversal/partial ALERTS now carry the exact share quantity to place, and the summary table adds a dollar P&L row at this size. Matches the STRATEGY's 'Share quantity' input — keep the two equal.")
slippage    = input.float(0.10, "Slippage Per Unit (charged on each exit)", step=0.01, group=grpE)

grpX = "Exit tuning (which apply depends on the Profile)"
maxCapOverride  = input.float(0.0,  "Max Stop override ($, 0 = use profile: C1=6 else 5)", step=0.5, group=grpX)
adaptiveTPScale = input.float(1.0,  "Adaptive TP — OR Width Multiplier (A1/B1)", step=0.05, group=grpX)
adaptiveTPMin   = input.float(2.14, "Adaptive TP — Minimum Floor $ (A1/B1)", step=0.01, group=grpX)
atrTPMult       = input.float(0.25, "ATR TP Multiplier x 14d ATR (C1)", step=0.01, group=grpX)
atrTPMin        = input.float(1.0,  "ATR TP Floor $ (C1)", step=0.25, group=grpX)
atrPeriod       = input.int(14,     "ATR Period (daily bars, C1)", minval=2, group=grpX)
fixedTP         = input.float(2.0,  "Fixed TP $ (C2)", step=0.25, group=grpX)
beTrigger       = input.float(0.55, "BE Retrace Trigger (% of OR width)", step=0.05, group=grpX)
beTrailAmt      = input.float(0.25, "BE Trail Amount ($)", step=0.01, group=grpX)
partialPct      = input.float(25.0, "Partial Exit Quantity % (A1/B1/C1)", step=1.0, group=grpX)
runnerMult      = input.float(0.75, "Runner Peak-Trail x OR width (A1)", step=0.05, group=grpX)
vwapArmProfit   = input.float(1.0,  "VWAP Cross — arm after profit $ (B1/C1)", step=0.25, group=grpX)
ttAtrPeriod     = input.int(5,      "ATR Trail — ATR Period (D1)", minval=1, group=grpX)
ttHhvPeriod     = input.int(10,     "ATR Trail — HHV/LLV Period (D1)", minval=1, group=grpX)
ttMult          = input.float(2.5,  "ATR Trail — ATR Multiplier (D1)", step=0.1, group=grpX, tooltip="D1 runner exit = the 'TRADE TASTIC' chandelier: line = HHV(high - mult*ATR(period), hhv) for longs (mirrored for shorts); the line moves only on a bar that CLOSES beyond it AND extends (close > prev close); the runner exits when a bar CLOSES across the line. Mult sweep 1.5-3.5 tested 2026-07-23: no setting wins 2024+2025+2026 together.")
exitOnClose     = input.bool(true,  "Close-triggered stop (stop fires only when the bar CLOSES beyond the level)", group=grpX, tooltip="ADOPTED 2026-07-14 (default ON): the stop fires only on a CLOSE beyond the level and fills at the close — skipping wick fakeouts. Walk-forward: +42-46% net and ~40% smaller drawdown vs the wick stop over 2022-2026 (flips 2024 positive). The TP still fills on a favorable wick. OFF = the old wick (any-touch) resting stop.")
beRealistic     = input.bool(true,  "Realistic resting stop: a BE-retrace can't protect its own firing bar", group=grpX, tooltip="ON (default) = matches a real broker + Python stop_fill_mode 'resting': moving the stop to break-even on the bar close only rests from the NEXT bar, so a bar that both fires the BE-retrace AND crashes to the base SL fills at the base SL. OFF = the old optimistic look-ahead (over-reports net ~40-45%).")

grpC = "Entry Confirmation"
confirmBreakout    = input.bool(false, "Require confirmation candle (2-candle break)", group=grpC)
requireTrendCandle = input.bool(true,  "Confirmation candle must be with-trend", group=grpC)

grpV = "Reversal"
revQtyMult = input.float(2.0, "Reversal Size Multiplier (before risk cap)", step=0.5, group=grpV)
revRiskCap = input.float(6.0, "Reversal Dollar-Risk Cap ($, 0=off)", step=0.5, group=grpV)

grpU = "Display"
showLabels = input.bool(true, "Show Entry/Exit Labels", group=grpU)
showLevels = input.bool(true, "Show OR / Trigger Levels", group=grpU)
showTable  = input.bool(true, "Show Summary Table", group=grpU)

maxCapSL = maxCapOverride > 0 ? maxCapOverride : (isC1 ? 6.0 : 5.0)

// ==================== PRIOR-DAY VOL + DAILY ATR (no repaint) ====================
f_priorRvol() =>
    r = ta.change(close) / close[1] * 100.0
    s = ta.stdev(r, volLookback, false)
    s[1]
rvol20 = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", f_priorRvol(), lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
f_priorATR() =>
    a = ta.sma(ta.tr(true), atrPeriod)
    a[1]
dailyATR = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", f_priorATR(), lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)

// ==================== "TRADE TASTIC" ATR TRAIL (D1 runner exit) ====================
// ONE line for BOTH directions, exactly the original script: TS = HHV(high - mult*ATR, hhv);
// it MOVES only on a bar that closes above the HHV AND extends (close > prev close) — else it
// holds. Color = close > TS. LONG runner exits on green->red (close <= TS); SHORT runner exits
// on red->green (close > TS) — after a waterfall the falling HHV drags the accepted level down,
// which is how the line comes back under price to catch the cover flip (2026-07-23: flip 10:35
// where the removed "mirror" line exited 11:55). First 16 bars pin to the close (script warm-up).
ttATR = ta.rma(ta.tr(true), ttAtrPeriod)
ttHHV = ta.highest(high - ttMult * ttATR, ttHhvPeriod)
var float ttTS = na
if bar_index < 16
    ttTS := close
else
    ttTS := close > ttHHV and close > close[1] ? ttHHV : ttTS

// ==================== STATE ====================
var float orHigh = na
var float orLow = na
var float orWidth = na
var bool skipVol = false
var bool skipWide = false
var bool daySkipped = false
var bool firstTaken = false
var bool active = false
var int tdir = 0
var float entry = na
var float stop = na
var float tp = na
var int entryBar = na
var bool inRev = false
var bool suppressPartial = false
var bool beTrig = false
var float beLevel = na
var bool part1 = false
var bool vwapArmed = false
var float qtyTotal = na
var float effQty = na
var float part1Pnl = 0.0
var float runnerPeak = na
var int primDir = 0
var bool primStopped = false
var float dayPnl = 0.0
var bool dayHasTrades = false
var int nTrades = 0
var int nSucc = 0
var int nFail = 0
var float netPnl = 0.0
var float grossP = 0.0
var float grossL = 0.0
var float worstDay = na
var float bestDay = na
var int totalDays = 0
var int tradeDays = 0
var int volSkipDays = 0
var int wideSkipDays = 0
var int cStop = 0
var int cWin = 0
var int cEOD = 0
var int cRev = 0

aEntryL = false
aEntryS = false
aRevL = false
aRevS = false
aBEFired = false
aPart = false
aWin = false
aStop = false
aEOD = false

// ==================== NEW DAY / OPENING RANGE ====================
isNewDay = session.isfirstbar_regular
isORbar = orStart == "09:45" ? (hour == 9 and minute == 45) : isNewDay
sessVwap = ta.vwap(hlc3, isNewDay)
isEODbar = (hour * 60 + minute) >= (eodHour * 60 + eodMin)
isLastBar = session.islastbar_regular          // half-day / early close: flatten on the session's LAST bar even if 15:50 never prints
isFlattenBar = isEODbar or isLastBar

if isNewDay
    if dayHasTrades
        worstDay := na(worstDay) ? dayPnl : math.min(worstDay, dayPnl)
        bestDay := na(bestDay) ? dayPnl : math.max(bestDay, dayPnl)
        tradeDays += 1
    totalDays += 1
    dayPnl := 0.0
    dayHasTrades := false
    orHigh := na
    orLow := na
    orWidth := na
    daySkipped := false
    firstTaken := false
    active := false
    tdir := 0
    entry := na
    stop := na
    tp := na
    entryBar := na
    inRev := false
    suppressPartial := false
    beTrig := false
    beLevel := na
    part1 := false
    vwapArmed := false
    qtyTotal := na
    effQty := na
    part1Pnl := 0.0
    runnerPeak := na
    primDir := 0
    primStopped := false

if isORbar
    orHigh := high
    orLow := low
    orWidth := high - low
    skipVol := not na(rvol20) and rvol20 > maxRvolPct
    skipWide := orWidth > maxORWidth
    daySkipped := skipVol or skipWide
    if skipVol
        volSkipDays += 1
    else if skipWide
        wideSkipDays += 1

longBrk = not na(orHigh) ? orHigh + orWidth * bufferPctOR / 100.0 : na
shortBrk = not na(orLow) ? orLow - orWidth * bufferPctOR / 100.0 : na
tpDist = tpModeSel == "Fixed" ? fixedTP : tpModeSel == "ORw" ? orWidth : tpModeSel == "ATR" ? (not na(dailyATR) ? math.max(atrTPMin, atrTPMult * dailyATR) : fixedTP) : (not na(orWidth) ? math.max(adaptiveTPMin, orWidth * adaptiveTPScale) : na)
canTrade = session.ismarket and not isORbar and not daySkipped and not na(orHigh) and not isFlattenBar and (not entryCutOn or hour * 60 + minute <= entryCutH * 60 + entryCutM)

longConfirm  = not confirmBreakout or (close[1] > longBrk and (close >= open or not requireTrendCandle))
shortConfirm = not confirmBreakout or (close[1] < shortBrk and (close <= open or not requireTrendCandle))

// ==================== PRIMARY ENTRY ====================
if canTrade and not active and not firstTaken
    if close > longBrk and longConfirm
        active := true
        tdir := 1
        inRev := false
        suppressPartial := false
        entry := close
        stop := maxCapSL > 0 ? math.max(orLow, close - maxCapSL) : orLow
        tp := close + tpDist
        beLevel := orHigh - beTrigger * orWidth
        entryBar := bar_index
        qtyTotal := tradeQty
        effQty := tradeQty
        part1 := false
        part1Pnl := 0.0
        beTrig := false
        runnerPeak := na
        vwapArmed := false
        primDir := 1
        firstTaken := true
        aEntryL := true
        if showLabels
            label.new(bar_index, low, "LONG " + str.tostring(entry, format.mintick), style=label.style_label_up, color=color.rgb(7,170,75), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
    else if close < shortBrk and shortConfirm
        active := true
        tdir := -1
        inRev := false
        suppressPartial := false
        entry := close
        stop := maxCapSL > 0 ? math.min(orHigh, close + maxCapSL) : orHigh
        tp := close - tpDist
        beLevel := orLow + beTrigger * orWidth
        entryBar := bar_index
        qtyTotal := tradeQty
        effQty := tradeQty
        part1 := false
        part1Pnl := 0.0
        beTrig := false
        runnerPeak := na
        vwapArmed := false
        primDir := -1
        firstTaken := true
        aEntryS := true
        if showLabels
            label.new(bar_index, high, "SHORT " + str.tostring(entry, format.mintick), style=label.style_label_down, color=color.rgb(243,76,76), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)

// ==================== REVERSAL ENTRY ====================
if canTrade and primStopped and not active
    if primDir == 1 and close < orLow
        rpu = math.abs(close - orHigh)
        rq = revRiskCap > 0 and rpu > 0 ? math.min(tradeQty * revQtyMult, revRiskCap / rpu) : tradeQty * revQtyMult
        active := true
        tdir := -1
        inRev := true
        suppressPartial := true
        entry := close
        stop := orHigh
        tp := na
        beLevel := orLow + beTrigger * orWidth
        entryBar := bar_index
        qtyTotal := rq
        effQty := rq
        part1 := false
        part1Pnl := 0.0
        beTrig := false
        runnerPeak := na
        primStopped := false
        cRev += 1
        aRevS := true
        if showLabels
            label.new(bar_index, high, "REV SHORT " + str.tostring(entry, format.mintick) + "\nqty " + str.tostring(rq, "#.##"), style=label.style_label_down, color=color.purple, textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
    else if primDir == -1 and close > orHigh
        rpu = math.abs(close - orLow)
        rq = revRiskCap > 0 and rpu > 0 ? math.min(tradeQty * revQtyMult, revRiskCap / rpu) : tradeQty * revQtyMult
        active := true
        tdir := 1
        inRev := true
        suppressPartial := true
        entry := close
        stop := orLow
        tp := na
        beLevel := orHigh - beTrigger * orWidth
        entryBar := bar_index
        qtyTotal := rq
        effQty := rq
        part1 := false
        part1Pnl := 0.0
        beTrig := false
        runnerPeak := na
        primStopped := false
        cRev += 1
        aRevL := true
        if showLabels
            label.new(bar_index, low, "REV LONG " + str.tostring(entry, format.mintick) + "\nqty " + str.tostring(rq, "#.##"), style=label.style_label_up, color=color.purple, textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)

// ==================== EXIT ENGINE (simulated; stop-first; never on the entry bar) ====================
if active and not na(stop) and bar_index > entryBar
    stopBarStart = stop        // the stop that was actually RESTING coming into this bar
    beFiredNow = false
    // Step 1: BE Retrace
    if not beTrig and not na(beLevel)
        if (tdir == 1 ? low <= beLevel : high >= beLevel)
            stop := tdir == 1 ? math.max(stop, entry) : math.min(stop, entry)
            beTrig := true
            aBEFired := true
            beFiredNow := true
    // Step 2: BE Trail
    if beTrig and beTrailAmt > 0
        stop := tdir == 1 ? math.max(stop, high - beTrailAmt) : math.min(stop, low + beTrailAmt)
    // Step 3: runner level (only after the partial, only for A1/B1/C1)
    runnerHit = false
    float runnerPx = na
    string runnerReason = "Trail"
    if usePartial and part1 and not suppressPartial and isD1
        // D1: TRADE TASTIC color flip — long exits close <= TS (green->red), short close > TS (red->green)
        if tdir == 1 ? close <= ttTS : close > ttTS
            runnerHit := true
            runnerPx := close
            runnerReason := "ATR Trail"
    else if usePartial and part1 and not suppressPartial and runnerVWAP
        if not vwapArmed and (tdir == 1 ? close - entry : entry - close) >= vwapArmProfit
            vwapArmed := true
        if vwapArmed and not na(sessVwap) and (tdir == 1 ? close <= sessVwap : close >= sessVwap)
            runnerHit := true
            runnerPx := close
            runnerReason := "VWAP Cross"
    else if usePartial and part1 and not suppressPartial and not runnerVWAP and runnerMult > 0
        if tdir == 1
            runnerPeak := na(runnerPeak) ? high : math.max(runnerPeak, high)
            lvl = runnerPeak - runnerMult * orWidth
            if exitOnClose ? close <= lvl : low <= lvl
                runnerHit := true
                runnerPx := exitOnClose ? close : lvl
        else
            runnerPeak := na(runnerPeak) ? low : math.min(runnerPeak, low)
            lvl = runnerPeak + runnerMult * orWidth
            if exitOnClose ? close >= lvl : high >= lvl
                runnerHit := true
                runnerPx := exitOnClose ? close : lvl
    // Step 4: hit checks — STOP FIRST (matches the engine), then target, then partial, then runner
    // resting-stop realism: a BE-retrace that fired THIS bar cannot protect it — fill against the
    // pre-retrace stop (the level actually resting coming into the bar).
    restStop = (beRealistic and beFiredNow) ? stopBarStart : stop
    // Close mode: trigger on the CLOSE beyond the CURRENT stop (be_lag is a wick-only concern), fill at close.
    // Wick mode: trigger on any touch of the be_lag resting stop, fill at the level (gap-aware).
    slHit = exitOnClose ? (tdir == 1 ? close <= stop : close >= stop) : (tdir == 1 ? low <= restStop : high >= restStop)
    slFill = exitOnClose ? close : (tdir == 1 ? math.min(restStop, open) : math.max(restStop, open))
    tpHit = not na(tp) and (tdir == 1 ? high >= tp : low <= tp)

    if slHit
        exitPx = slFill
        perUnit = tdir == 1 ? (exitPx - entry - slippage) : (entry - exitPx - slippage)
        pnlTotal = perUnit * effQty + part1Pnl
        isBETrail = beTrig and (tdir == 1 ? exitPx > entry : exitPx < entry)
        reason = beTrig ? (isBETrail ? "BE Trail" : "BE Stop") : "Base SL"
        cStop += 1
        aStop := true
        nTrades += 1
        if pnlTotal > 0
            nSucc += 1
            grossP += pnlTotal
        else
            nFail += 1
            grossL += math.abs(pnlTotal)
        netPnl += pnlTotal
        dayPnl += pnlTotal
        dayHasTrades := true
        if not inRev
            // Arms on the STOP-HIT bar (immediate), so the reversal fires on the NEXT bar (N+1) - matches
            // orb_engine.py L933 and the v3 STRATEGY (whose de-sync/arming was reordered 2026-07-13 to also
            // arm on N+1). Base SL / BE Stop / BE Trail arm; peak-trail ("Trail") / VWAP / TP / EOD do not.
            primStopped := true
        if showLabels
            label.new(bar_index, tdir == 1 ? low : high, (inRev ? "REV " : "") + reason + " " + str.tostring(exitPx, format.mintick) + "\n" + (pnlTotal >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(pnlTotal, "#.##"), style=tdir == 1 ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color=isBETrail ? color.rgb(7,170,75) : color.orange, textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
        active := false
        tdir := 0
        inRev := false
        tp := na
        stop := na
    else if usePartial and tpHit and not part1
        // D1 full-trail mode: the target touch only ARMS the trail — nothing is closed here
        p1qty = d1FullTrail ? 0.0 : qtyTotal * partialPct / 100.0
        pu = tdir == 1 ? (tp - entry - slippage) : (entry - tp - slippage)
        part1Pnl := pu * p1qty
        effQty := qtyTotal - p1qty
        part1 := true
        if not d1FullTrail
            aPart := true
            if showLabels
                label.new(bar_index, tdir == 1 ? high : low, "PARTIAL " + str.tostring(partialPct, "#") + "% @ " + str.tostring(tp, format.mintick) + "\n+" + str.tostring(part1Pnl, "#.##"), style=tdir == 1 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up, color=color.rgb(7,170,75), textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny)
        else if showLabels
            label.new(bar_index, tdir == 1 ? high : low, "TRAIL ARMED @ " + str.tostring(tp, format.mintick), style=tdir == 1 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up, color=color.new(color.yellow, 30), textcolor=color.black, size=size.tiny)
        tp := na
    else if (not usePartial) and tpHit
        // C2 full exit at the target
        exitPx = tp
        perUnit = tdir == 1 ? (exitPx - entry - slippage) : (entry - exitPx - slippage)
        pnlTotal = perUnit * effQty
        cWin += 1
        aWin := true
        nTrades += 1
        if pnlTotal > 0
            nSucc += 1
            grossP += pnlTotal
        else
            nFail += 1
            grossL += math.abs(pnlTotal)
        netPnl += pnlTotal
        dayPnl += pnlTotal
        dayHasTrades := true
        if showLabels
            label.new(bar_index, tdir == 1 ? high : low, (inRev ? "REV " : "") + "TP " + str.tostring(exitPx, format.mintick) + "\n+" + str.tostring(pnlTotal, "#.##"), style=tdir == 1 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up, color=color.new(color.lime, 0), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
        active := false
        tdir := 0
        inRev := false
        tp := na
        stop := na
    else if runnerHit
        exitPx = runnerPx
        perUnit = tdir == 1 ? (exitPx - entry - slippage) : (entry - exitPx - slippage)
        pnlTotal = perUnit * effQty + part1Pnl
        cWin += 1
        aWin := true
        nTrades += 1
        if pnlTotal > 0
            nSucc += 1
            grossP += pnlTotal
        else
            nFail += 1
            grossL += math.abs(pnlTotal)
        netPnl += pnlTotal
        dayPnl += pnlTotal
        dayHasTrades := true
        if showLabels
            label.new(bar_index, tdir == 1 ? high : low, (inRev ? "REV " : "") + runnerReason + " " + str.tostring(exitPx, format.mintick) + "\n" + (pnlTotal >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(pnlTotal, "#.##"), style=tdir == 1 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up, color=color.new(color.aqua, 0), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
        active := false
        tdir := 0
        inRev := false
        tp := na
        stop := na

// ==================== EOD FORCED CLOSE (all profiles; half-day = session last bar) ====================
if active and isFlattenBar and tdir != 0
    exitPx = close
    perUnit = tdir == 1 ? (exitPx - entry - slippage) : (entry - exitPx - slippage)
    pnlTotal = perUnit * effQty + part1Pnl
    cEOD += 1
    aEOD := true
    nTrades += 1
    if pnlTotal > 0
        nSucc += 1
        grossP += pnlTotal
    else
        nFail += 1
        grossL += math.abs(pnlTotal)
    netPnl += pnlTotal
    dayPnl += pnlTotal
    dayHasTrades := true
    if showLabels
        label.new(bar_index, close, (inRev ? "REV EOD " : "EOD ") + str.tostring(exitPx, format.mintick) + "\n" + (pnlTotal >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(pnlTotal, "#.##"), style=label.style_label_left, color=color.rgb(255,140,0), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
    active := false
    tdir := 0
    inRev := false
    tp := na
    stop := na

// ==================== VISUALS ====================
plot(showLevels and not daySkipped and not na(orHigh) ? orHigh : na, "OR High", color=color.new(color.aqua, 0), style=plot.style_linebr)
plot(showLevels and not daySkipped and not na(orLow) ? orLow : na, "OR Low", color=color.new(color.aqua, 0), style=plot.style_linebr)
plot(showLevels and not daySkipped and not na(longBrk) ? longBrk : na, "Long Trigger", color=color.new(color.lime, 0), style=plot.style_linebr)
plot(showLevels and not daySkipped and not na(shortBrk) ? shortBrk : na, "Short Trigger", color=color.new(color.red, 0), style=plot.style_linebr)
plot(active ? stop : na, "Active Stop", color=color.red, linewidth=2, style=plot.style_linebr)
plot(active and not na(tp) ? tp : na, "Active TP", color=color.lime, linewidth=2, style=plot.style_linebr)
plot(active and not beTrig and not na(beLevel) ? beLevel : na, "BE Trigger", color=color.new(color.yellow, 0), style=plot.style_circles)
plot(primStopped and not active ? (primDir == 1 ? orLow : orHigh) : na, "Reversal Trigger", color=color.new(color.purple, 0), linewidth=2, style=plot.style_circles)
plot(isD1 and active and part1 ? ttTS : na, "ATR Trail (D1 runner)", color=color.new(color.yellow, 0), linewidth=2, style=plot.style_linebr)
bgcolor(daySkipped ? color.new(color.gray, 90) : na, title="Day skipped")

// ==================== ALERTS ====================
if barstate.isconfirmed
    base = " | " + str.substring(profile, 0, 2) + " | " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period + "m | Px $" + str.tostring(close, "#.##") + " | " + str.format_time(time, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm", "America/New_York") + " ET"
    entryShares = math.round(tradeQty * shareQty)
    revShares   = math.round(nz(qtyTotal, tradeQty) * shareQty)        // qtyTotal = risk-parity size on reversal bars
    partShares  = math.round(nz(qtyTotal, tradeQty) * shareQty * partialPct / 100)
    if aEntryL
        alert("[ENTRY] LONG breakout — BUY " + str.tostring(entryShares) + " sh at market" + base, alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    if aEntryS
        alert("[ENTRY] SHORT breakout — SELL SHORT " + str.tostring(entryShares) + " sh at market" + base, alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    if aRevL
        alert("[ENTRY-REV] REVERSAL LONG (risk-parity size) — BUY " + str.tostring(revShares) + " sh at market" + base, alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    if aRevS
        alert("[ENTRY-REV] REVERSAL SHORT (risk-parity size) — SELL SHORT " + str.tostring(revShares) + " sh at market" + base, alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    if aBEFired
        alert("[STATE] BE RETRACE FIRED — move stop to ENTRY" + base, alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    if aPart
        alert("[EXIT-PARTIAL] " + str.tostring(partialPct, "#") + "% closed at target (" + str.tostring(partShares) + " sh); runner now governs" + base, alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    if aWin
        alert("[EXIT-WIN] target / runner exit — close remaining position" + base, alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    if aStop
        alert("[EXIT-STOP] stop hit — close position (Base SL / BE Stop / BE Trail)" + base, alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    if aEOD
        alert("[EXIT-EOD] End-of-day forced close" + base, alert.freq_once_per_bar)

// ==================== NAMED ALERTS — per Profile x Status (pick in TradingView's "Add alert" dialog) ==========
// The alert() calls above fire the single generic "Any alert() function call". The alertcondition() calls
// below add NAMED, individually-selectable alerts. Each is gated by the SELECTED profile, so only your active
// profile's alerts can ever fire (on a B1 chart the A1/C1/C2 rows stay silent). Set frequency "Once Per Bar Close".
// --- A1 · Adaptive + Peak-Trail ---
alertcondition(isA1 and aEntryL,  title="A1 Buy",      message="A1 BUY - long breakout, buy at market | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isA1 and aEntryS,  title="A1 Sell",     message="A1 SELL - short breakout, sell short at market | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isA1 and aRevL,    title="A1 Rev Buy",  message="A1 REVERSAL BUY - risk-parity long at market | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isA1 and aRevS,    title="A1 Rev Sell", message="A1 REVERSAL SELL - risk-parity short at market | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isA1 and aBEFired, title="A1 BE",       message="A1 BREAK-EVEN - move stop to entry | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isA1 and aPart,    title="A1 Partial",  message="A1 PARTIAL - 25% closed at target; runner governs | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isA1 and aWin,     title="A1 TP",       message="A1 TP - close remaining (target/runner win) | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isA1 and aStop,    title="A1 SL",       message="A1 SL - close position (stop hit) | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isA1 and aEOD,     title="A1 EOD",      message="A1 EOD - end-of-day forced close | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
// --- B1 · Adaptive + VWAP runner ---
alertcondition(isB1 and aEntryL,  title="B1 Buy",      message="B1 BUY - long breakout, buy at market | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isB1 and aEntryS,  title="B1 Sell",     message="B1 SELL - short breakout, sell short at market | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isB1 and aRevL,    title="B1 Rev Buy",  message="B1 REVERSAL BUY - risk-parity long at market | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isB1 and aRevS,    title="B1 Rev Sell", message="B1 REVERSAL SELL - risk-parity short at market | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isB1 and aBEFired, title="B1 BE",       message="B1 BREAK-EVEN - move stop to entry | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isB1 and aPart,    title="B1 Partial",  message="B1 PARTIAL - 25% closed at target; runner governs | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isB1 and aWin,     title="B1 TP",       message="B1 TP - close remaining (VWAP-cross / runner win) | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isB1 and aStop,    title="B1 SL",       message="B1 SL - close position (stop hit) | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isB1 and aEOD,     title="B1 EOD",      message="B1 EOD - end-of-day forced close | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
// --- C1 · ATR 0.25 + 25% Partial + VWAP ---
alertcondition(isC1 and aEntryL,  title="C1 Buy",      message="C1 BUY - long breakout, buy at market | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isC1 and aEntryS,  title="C1 Sell",     message="C1 SELL - short breakout, sell short at market | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isC1 and aRevL,    title="C1 Rev Buy",  message="C1 REVERSAL BUY - risk-parity long at market | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isC1 and aRevS,    title="C1 Rev Sell", message="C1 REVERSAL SELL - risk-parity short at market | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isC1 and aBEFired, title="C1 BE",       message="C1 BREAK-EVEN - move stop to entry | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isC1 and aPart,    title="C1 Partial",  message="C1 PARTIAL - 25% closed at target; runner governs | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isC1 and aWin,     title="C1 TP",       message="C1 TP - close remaining (VWAP-cross / runner win) | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isC1 and aStop,    title="C1 SL",       message="C1 SL - close position (stop hit) | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isC1 and aEOD,     title="C1 EOD",      message="C1 EOD - end-of-day forced close | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
// --- D1 · Adaptive + ATR-Trail runner (experimental) ---
alertcondition(isD1 and aEntryL,  title="D1 Buy",      message="D1 BUY - long breakout, buy at market | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isD1 and aEntryS,  title="D1 Sell",     message="D1 SELL - short breakout, sell short at market | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isD1 and aRevL,    title="D1 Rev Buy",  message="D1 REVERSAL BUY - risk-parity long at market | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isD1 and aRevS,    title="D1 Rev Sell", message="D1 REVERSAL SELL - risk-parity short at market | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isD1 and aBEFired, title="D1 BE",       message="D1 BREAK-EVEN - move stop to entry | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isD1 and aPart,    title="D1 Partial",  message="D1 PARTIAL - 25% closed at target; ATR trail governs | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isD1 and aWin,     title="D1 TP",       message="D1 TP - close remaining (ATR-trail / runner win) | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isD1 and aStop,    title="D1 SL",       message="D1 SL - close position (stop hit) | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isD1 and aEOD,     title="D1 EOD",      message="D1 EOD - end-of-day forced close | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
// --- C2 · OR-Width Full-Exit (no partial; was fixed $2 pre-v3.5) ---
alertcondition(isC2 and aEntryL,  title="C2 Buy",      message="C2 BUY - long breakout, buy at market | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isC2 and aEntryS,  title="C2 Sell",     message="C2 SELL - short breakout, sell short at market | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isC2 and aRevL,    title="C2 Rev Buy",  message="C2 REVERSAL BUY - risk-parity long at market | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isC2 and aRevS,    title="C2 Rev Sell", message="C2 REVERSAL SELL - risk-parity short at market | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isC2 and aBEFired, title="C2 BE",       message="C2 BREAK-EVEN - move stop to entry | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isC2 and aWin,     title="C2 TP",       message="C2 TP - close position (OR-width target win) | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isC2 and aStop,    title="C2 SL",       message="C2 SL - close position (stop hit) | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(isC2 and aEOD,     title="C2 EOD",      message="C2 EOD - end-of-day forced close | {{ticker}} {{interval}}m @ {{close}}")

// ==================== SUMMARY TABLE ====================
var table tbl = table.new(position.top_right, 2, 16, border_width=1)
f_row(_r, _k, _v, _col) =>
    table.cell(tbl, 0, _r, _k, text_color=color.white, bgcolor=color.rgb(25,25,25), text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, _r, _v, text_color=_col, bgcolor=color.rgb(25,25,25), text_size=size.small)
if barstate.islast and showTable
    wD = dayHasTrades ? (na(worstDay) ? dayPnl : math.min(worstDay, dayPnl)) : worstDay
    bD = dayHasTrades ? (na(bestDay) ? dayPnl : math.max(bestDay, dayPnl)) : bestDay
    tD = tradeDays + (dayHasTrades ? 1 : 0)
    wr = nTrades > 0 ? nSucc * 100.0 / nTrades : 0.0
    pf = grossL > 0 ? grossP / grossL : na
    exp = nTrades > 0 ? netPnl / nTrades : 0.0
    table.cell(tbl, 0, 0, "UDB-ORB v3.9.1", text_color=color.white, bgcolor=color.rgb(30,30,50), text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 0, str.substring(profile, 0, 2) + " · " + tpModeSel, text_color=color.aqua, bgcolor=color.rgb(30,30,50), text_size=size.small)
    f_row(1, "Trades", str.tostring(nTrades), color.yellow)
    f_row(2, "Win Rate", str.tostring(wr, "#.#") + "%", color.orange)
    f_row(3, "Net P&L (per unit)", (netPnl >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(netPnl, "#.##"), netPnl >= 0 ? color.lime : color.red)
    f_row(4, "Profit Factor", na(pf) ? "n/a" : str.tostring(pf, "#.##"), na(pf) ? color.silver : (pf >= 1 ? color.lime : color.red))
    f_row(5, "Expectancy", (exp >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(exp, "#.###"), exp >= 0 ? color.lime : color.red)
    f_row(6, "Best / Worst Day", (na(bD) ? "-" : "+" + str.tostring(bD, "#.##")) + " / " + (na(wD) ? "-" : str.tostring(wD, "#.##")), color.silver)
    f_row(7, "Trade Days", str.tostring(tD) + " / " + str.tostring(totalDays), color.aqua)
    f_row(8, "Today's TP dist", na(tpDist) ? "n/a" : "$" + str.tostring(tpDist, "#.##"), color.aqua)
    f_row(9, "Max Stop", "$" + str.tostring(maxCapSL, "#"), color.silver)
    f_row(10, "Skipped vol / wide", str.tostring(volSkipDays) + " / " + str.tostring(wideSkipDays), color.fuchsia)
    f_row(11, "Reversals", str.tostring(cRev), color.purple)
    f_row(12, "Wins (TP/runner)", str.tostring(cWin), color.lime)
    f_row(13, "Stops", str.tostring(cStop), color.orange)
    f_row(14, "EOD closes", str.tostring(cEOD), color.silver)
    f_row(15, "Net @ " + str.tostring(shareQty) + " sh", (netPnl >= 0 ? "+$" : "-$") + str.tostring(math.abs(netPnl * shareQty), "#,###"), netPnl >= 0 ? color.lime : color.red)
